 "swaps": [
  {
   "from": "kale",
   "to": "watercress",
   "verdict": "Watercress is often said to beat kale on nutrients and fibre. It doesn't. Per 100 g (USDA), kale has more of every nutrient listed here, including fibre (4.1 g vs 0.5 g), iron (1.6 vs 0.2 mg) and folate (62 vs 9 ug). What watercress does win on is price: about RM11/kg against RM47/kg from the same Cameron seller, so each ringgit buys more calcium, vitamin C, vitamin A, vitamin K, potassium and protein. Kale still gives more fibre, iron and folate per ringgit.",
   "wins": [
    "protein per RM",
    "calcium per RM",
    "vitC per RM",
    "vitA per RM",
    "vitK per RM",
    "potassium per RM"
   ],
